the tyrosine phosphorylation of the T cell receptor subunits and ZAP-70 in murine thymocytes</article-title><source>J Exp Med</source><year>1996</year><volume>183</volume><fpage>1053</fpage><lpage>1062</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8642247</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1084/jem.183.3.1053</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Negishi</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Motoyama</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Nakayama</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Nakayama</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Senju</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Hatakeyama</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Zhang</surname><given-names>Q</given-names></name><name><surname>Chan</surname><given-names>AC</given-names></name><name><surname>Loh</surname><given-names>DY</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Essential role for ZAP-70 in both positive and negative selection of thymocytes</article-title><source>Nature</source><year>1995</year><volume>376</volume><fpage>435</fpage><lpage>438</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7630421</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/376435a0</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McManus</surname><given-names>MT</given-names></name><name><surname>Sharp</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Gene silencing in mammals by small interfering RNAs</article-title><source>Nat Rev Genet</source><year>2002</year><volume>3</volume><fpage>737</fpage><lpage>747</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12360232</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/nrg908</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mao</surname><given